  "final_text": "Wrote `impact.txt` at the repo root with the five definitions whose bodies use `resolve_color_default`:\n\n```\nsrc/click/exceptions.py#ClickException.__init__\nsrc/click/termui.py#_readline_prompt\nsrc/click/termui.py#get_pager_file\nsrc/click/termui.py#progressbar\nsrc/click/utils.py#echo\n```\n\nHow I got there:\n- `who` on `src/click/globals.py#resolve_color_default` returned nine backlinks; I dropped the three module-level ones (bare `from .globals import \u2026` in `exceptions.py`, `termui.py`, `utils.py`) and the `ClickException` class-page entry, since resolving the class showed the call is inside `__init__`, not the class body. Spot-checking `termui.echo_via_pager` and `termui.secho` confirmed the index's per-definition refs match the source.\n- Tests: the index derives no refs for files under `tests/` (verified \u2014 `tests/test_compat.py`'s `from click._compat import strip_ansi` produces an empty `refs` list), so `who` can't answer for them. I read the test files that could plausibly touch color/echo/pager/prompt resolution: `test_termui.py` (whole file), `test_compat.py`, `test_testing.py`, `test_context.py`, `test_stream_lifecycle.py`, `test_imports.py`, `conftest.py`, and `test_utils/{test_echo,test_style,test_echo_via_pager,test_confirm,test_prompt}.py`. None mentions the name. A `search` for `color` across all indexed pages also turned up no other test whose name or docstring touches color, so nothing pointed at the remaining test modules (options/arguments/commands/types/formatting/completion, etc.).\n\nCaveat worth stating plainly: I could not run a text search (shell readers are denied here, and the cttp index only matches names/signatures/docstrings plus package-level refs), so the test side rests on targeted reading rather than an exhaustive grep of `tests/`. If you want certainty there, a `grep -rn resolve_color_default tests/` would confirm it in one shot.",
